    "title": "DEA conducts investigation at multiple locations in Orange County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chelsea Hylton Zach Boetto ,\n10 hours ago\nDEA conducts several drug enforcement operations across Orange County 02:54\nThe Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) is conducting an investigation at multiple locations in Orange County on Wednesday morning.\nA spokesperson for the DEA Los Angeles Field Division did not provide details on the locations or the reason for the investigation, since it is ongoing, but said that all of the operations were connected.\nAerial footage showed several agents at a residence in the 30 block of Brisbane Court in Tustin, where agents allegedly discovered a drug lab. They were seen removing several large pieces of machinery from the home's garage as part of what they said was a much larger investigation.\nAgents also removed several bags labeled \"Firmapress,\" which is apparently an \"all-in-one pill mix.\"\nThe DEA also confirmed agents investigated a location in Irvine, but did not provide further details. Aerial footage showed agents walking in and out of a home on Steeplechase, where a federal search warrant was served for an ongoing drug investigation.\nThe two properties are separated by approximately 8 miles.\nAuthorities did not note if any arrests were made, but neighbors said that one person was seen being taken away in handcuffs.",
    "summary": "By Chelsea Hylton Zach Boetto , DEA conducts several drug enforcement operations across Orange County 02:54 The Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) is conducting an investigation at multiple locations in Orange County on Wednesday morning. A spokesperson for the DEA Los Angeles Field Division did not provide details on the locations or the reason for the investigation, since it is ongoing, but said that all of the operations were connected. They were seen removing several large pieces of machinery from the home's garage as part of what they said was a much larger investigation.",
